MASTER AESTHETIC & SYSTEM RULES FOR TUI_OS (VAULT WORLDWIDE):
Full language: docs/LANGUAGE.md — portable BLACK LANTERN canon (tokens, vetoes, SPECK, take/leave). Obey that file.
Overnight agent brief: docs/OVERNIGHT_PROMPT.md.

This is one continuous personal OS field — not a dashboard, not stacked sections.
No cards, rounded corners, soft shadows, section billboards, DateBlocks, or teal watermarks.

PALETTE: Field #000000 · Paper #F4F4F0 · Cobalt #0000FF.
Cobalt = spine, selection invert, dossier overlay. Paper = type. Urgent red only for strike / URGENT.
No harvest amber. No charcoal leather. No globe seal.

TYPE: Helvetica Neue / Helvetica / Arial. No JetBrains. No Space Grotesk.

COMPOSITION (desktop field, not a PWA, not mobile-first):
1. Composed SPECK canvas. Organs are placed ink (PLACE), not CSS regions.
2. PIPE is the split-page binder: FOCUS left (backlog / active), GATEWAY right (staging / done), ASCII spine. Shovel advances a task. Empty ledger rows stay.
3. NEST is the unix pit. CLIP a stem into PIPE as a TASK. DUMP is scratch tape.
4. HIT a TASK → cobalt dossier CHIP drops from that row. Tap row / field / other organ to dismiss.
5. ONE one-line dock, locked to viewport bottom. Never three forms. Never header CTX tabs (PROJECTS / ROSTER / FLEET / LOGS).

HARD VETO: DateBlocks, jagged day cards, SaaS kanban cards, amber theme, JSON-as-database, second prompt.
Do not revive the globe seal, beige cassette chrome, month-as-OS, or a Tailwind binder.
